#: src/ai/rules.md:1
msgid "Using Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:3
msgid ""
"Rules are prompts inserted at the beginning of each agent interaction. Add "
"them via files in your worktree (`.rules`, etc.) or through the Rules "
"Library for reuse across projects and threads."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:5
msgid "`.rules` files"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:7
msgid ""
"Zed supports including `.rules` files at the top level of worktrees, and "
"they act as project-level instructions that are included in all of your "
"interactions with the Agent Panel. Other names for this file are also "
"supported for compatibility with other agents, but note that the first file "
"which matches in this list will be used:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:10
msgid "`.rules`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:11
msgid "`.cursorrules`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:12
msgid "`.windsurfrules`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:13
msgid "`.clinerules`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:14
msgid "`.github/copilot-instructions.md`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:15
msgid "`AGENT.md`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:16
msgid "`AGENTS.md`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:17
msgid "`CLAUDE.md`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:18
msgid "`GEMINI.md`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:20
msgid "Rules Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:22
msgid ""
"The Rules Library is an interface for writing and managing rules. It's a "
"full editor with syntax highlighting and all standard keybindings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:24
msgid ""
"You can use the inline assistant right in the rules editor, allowing you to "
"automate and rewrite rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:26
msgid "Opening the Rules Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:28
msgid "Open the Agent Panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:29
msgid "Click on the Agent menu (`...`) in the top right corner."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:30
msgid "Select `Rules...` from the dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:32
msgid ""
"You can also reach it by running <code class=\"hljs\">agent: open rules "
"library</code> in the command palette or through the <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-l|ctrl-alt-l</kbd> keybinding."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:34
msgid "Managing Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:36
msgid ""
"Once a rules file is selected, you can edit it directly in the built-in "
"editor. Its title can be changed from the editor title bar as well."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:38
msgid ""
"Rules can be duplicated, deleted, or added to the default rules using the "
"buttons in the rules editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:40
msgid "Creating Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:42
msgid ""
"To create a rule file, simply open the `Rules Library` and click the `+` "
"button. Rules files are stored locally and can be accessed from the library "
"at any time."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:44
msgid "For guidance on writing effective rules:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:46
msgid ""
"[Anthropic: Prompt Engineering](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-"
"with-claude/prompt-engineering/overview)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:47
msgid ""
"[OpenAI: Prompt Engineering](https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/prompt-"
"engineering)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:49
msgid "Editing the Default Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:51
msgid ""
"Zed allows you to customize the default rules used when interacting with "
"LLMs. Or to be more precise, it uses a series of rules that are combined to "
"form the default rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:54
msgid ""
"Default rules are included in the context of every new thread automatically. "
"You can also manually add other rules (that are not flagged as default) as "
"context using the `@rule` command."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:57
msgid "Migrating from Prompt Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:59
msgid ""
"Previously, the Rules Library was called the \"Prompt Library\". The new "
"rules system replaces the Prompt Library except in a few specific cases, "
"which are outlined below."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:62
msgid "Slash Commands in Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:64
msgid ""
"Previously, it was possible to use slash commands (now @-mentions) in custom "
"prompts (now rules). There is currently no support for using @-mentions in "
"rules files, however, slash commands are supported in rules files when used "
"with text threads. See the documentation for using [slash commands in rules]"
"(./text-threads.md#slash-commands-in-rules) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:68
msgid "Prompt templates"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:70
msgid ""
"Zed maintains backwards compatibility with its original template system, "
"which allows you to customize prompts used throughout the application, "
"including the inline assistant. While the Rules Library is now the primary "
"way to manage prompts, you can still use these legacy templates to override "
"default prompts. For more details, see the [Rules Templates](./text-threads."
"md#rule-templates) section under [Text Threads](./text-threads.md)."
msgstr ""
